  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">MHPSS Jemen 2024 &#x2013; WHO MHPSS Technical Working Group Coordinator</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Yemen is currently facing the world&apos;s largest humanitarian crisis, with approximately 18.2 million people in need of some form of assistance to survive. The ongoing conflict has exacerbated the mental health and psychosocial support (MHPSS) needs of the Yemeni population. The impacts of this devastating war are farreaching, affecting the mental wellbeing and psychosocial resilience of individuals and communities across the country.The working group (TWG) is committed to working in collaboration with all stakeholders, including government agencies, international organizations and local non-governmental organizations (NGOs), to ensure a holistic and effective response to the crisis by bringing together Health, Protection and Education actors in the country. To this end, the TWG requires an experienced MHPSS specialist to support the TWG to ensure coordination in Aden, Yemen.</narrative>
  </description>
